    <briefdescription>
<para>This class can be used for tracking most instruction setters. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The two template arguments are:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>GetterFn: The getter member function pointer (e.g., <computeroutput>&amp;Foo::get</computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>SetterFn: The setter member function pointer (e.g., <computeroutput>&amp;Foo::set</computeroutput>) Upon construction, it saves a copy of the original value by calling the getter function. Revert sets the value back to the one saved, using the setter function provided.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Example: Tracker.track(std::make_unique&lt;
               GenericSetter&lt;&amp;FooInst::get, &amp;FooInst::set&gt;&gt;(I, Tracker)); </para>
    </detaileddescription>
